<title>UK: GEC gains as France eases on Framatome tie.</title>
<headline>GEC gains as France eases on Framatome tie.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in General Electric Co Plc advanced in brisk trading on Friday as the market took the view that the French government's attitude to cross-border links involving its strategic industries was softening, analysts said.</p>
<p>The stock rose 4p to 374-1/2p with nearly five million shares traded after France said GEC could join a proposed alliance between Framatome Connectors and Alcatel Alsthom, in its energy activities.</p>
<p>&quot;GEC has suffered rebuffs from France and any signs that suggest a rapprochement between France and GEC on the power or defence side looks good to the market,&quot; said one anaylst.</p>
</text>
